<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!DOCTYPE html []><html lang="en"><head><title>WSR 26-19-116 (26-19)</title></head><body><!-- field: WSRNumber --><div style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold;margin-top:0.5in;margin-bottom:0pt;">WSR 26-19-116</div><!-- field: --><!-- field: WSRRegType --><div style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">PROPOSED RULES</div><!-- field: --><!-- field: WSRAgencyName --><div style="text-align:center;font-weight:bold;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE</div><!-- field: --><div style="text-align:center;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:12pt;font-size:8pt;">[Filed September 22, 2026, 9:22 a.m.]</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Original Notice.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Preproposal statement of inquiry was filed as WSR 26-15-114.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Title of Rule and Other Identifying Information: Chapter 365-212 WAC, manufactured/mobile home relocation assistance program rules repeal.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Hearing Location(s): On November 4, 2026, at 11:00 a.m. to 12:00 p.m., online/virtual via Zoom at <span>https://wastatecommerce.zoom.us/j/82462204210?pwd=SlmubAmmbPi6sZMNafN2jNOyeSzkoY.1</span>, Meeting ID 824 6220 4210, Passcode 025225. This hearing is open to the public. Registration is required at <span>https://wastatecommerce.zoom.us/meeting/register/_wyocHHuTiKPiwTLY_KBNQ</span>.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Date of Intended Adoption: November 6, 2026.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Submit Written Comments to: Augustine Robinson, 1500 Jefferson Street S.E., [Olympia, WA 98501,] email <span>augustine.robinson@commerce.wa.gov</span>, beginning October 7, 2026, 5:00 p.m., by November 4, 2026, 5:00 p.m.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Assistance for Persons with Disabilities: Contact Augustine Robinson, phone 564-669-4930, email <span>augustine.robinson@commerce.wa.gov</span>, by October 28, 2026, 5:00 p.m.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Purpose of the Proposal and Its Anticipated Effects, Including Any Changes in Existing Rules: This rule making will repeal WAC 365-212-010 through 365-212-090.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Reasons Supporting Proposal: These rules are obsolete and inaccurate due to statute and programmatic changes since they were established in 2003. Incorrect information about the program and its operations can lead to confusion and potential legal risks since they do not reflect the current statutes.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Statutory Authority for Adoption: RCW  <a href="http://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=43.330.040">43.330.040</a> Director powers and duties.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Rule is not necessitated by federal law, federal or state court decision.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Name of Proponent: Department of commerce, governmental.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Name of Agency Personnel Responsible for Drafting: Augustine Robinson, 1500 Jefferson Street S.E., Olympia, WA 98501, 564-669-4930; Implementation and Enforcement: Lisa Sohni, 1500 Jefferson Street S.E., Olympia, WA 98501, 206-613-7557.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">A school district fiscal impact statement is not required under RCW  <a href="http://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=28A.305.135">28A.305.135</a>.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">A cost-benefit analysis is not required under RCW  <a href="http://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=34.05.328">34.05.328</a>.</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">This rule proposal, or portions of the proposal, is exempt from requirements of the Regulatory Fairness Act because the proposal: </div><div style="text-indent:-25px;padding-left:25px;margin-left:0.5in;margin-right:0pt;">Is exempt under RCW  <a href="http://app.leg.wa.gov/RCW/default.aspx?cite=19.85.025">19.85.025</a>(4).</div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">Scope of exemption for rule proposal:</div><div style="text-indent:1in;">Is fully exempt.</div><div style="text-align:right;margin-top:4.5pt;text-indent:0.5in;">September 22, 2026</div><div style="text-align:right;text-indent:0.5in;">Amanda Hathaway</div><div style="text-align:right;text-indent:0.5in;">Rules Coordinator</div><div>RDS-7325.1</div><div style="margin-top:0.1in;"><span style="text-decoration:underline;">REPEALER</span><span style="padding-left:10px;" /></div><div style="text-indent:0.5in;">The following sections of the Washington Administrative Code are repealed:</div><table style="width:432pt;border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0.5in;font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:10pt;"><colgroup><col style="width:144pt;" /><col style="width:288pt;" /></colgroup><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-010</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">What definitions apply to this chapter?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-020</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">How do I contact the office of manufactured housing?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-030</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">Who is eligible to receive relocation assistance?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-040</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">What constitutes a completed application?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-050</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">If I meet the requirements, how much assistance could I be eligible for?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-060</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">What expenses are allowable for reimbursement?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-070</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">What documentation must I provide as adequate proof a home cannot be relocated?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-080</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">What documentation must I provide to be reimbursed for a down payment on another home?</div></td></tr><tr><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">WAC 365-212-090</div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;"><div style="padding-left:0pt;padding-right:0pt;">What criteria is used to determine park-owner fraud?</div></td></tr></table></body></html>